#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096417 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d7a77a89-0535-54da-a246-36ee5b4e9e7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3634" :question/problem "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096418 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096618 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15a60dd-f6a7-577d-bdbc-148032de94c8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing an Exponential or Logarithmic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6bb0eded-7277-5ab5-8c13-bfc480403b1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3635" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=x^2\\ln x,$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}ln⁡x+{x}^{2}{(ln⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot ln⁡x+{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2xln⁡x+x \\\\  & =x(2ln⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee64135e-9b9f-5429-a4df-efa522042b83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Product  at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "072ce609-b04d-57b0-9c7d-cbb8765c38fa" :question/math-academy-id "e-3636" :question/problem "If a curve $\\mathcal C$ is given by $y=e^x\\sin x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\dfrac \\pi 2.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x) = e^x$ and $v(x)=\\sin{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = e^x,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos x.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot cos⁡x+sin⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(cos⁡x+sin⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\dfrac\\pi 2$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi /2} & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(cos⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+sin⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(0+1) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $e^{\\pi/2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329a0351-2458-5dc2-afb3-fb83d076e70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}sec⁡x+{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285251} {:answer/id #uuid "3d41ba8e-fd4a-5c5b-8e2c-3eb30e482c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285366} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2ff268-76d1-583f-9abe-62b917b9c7eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{csc}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285621} {:answer/id #uuid "93783351-25ff-5c87-8ae9-958c98c327e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286129} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44b9e2e-ea9e-5094-bc4f-bc781e7df5d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a541e9ea-7fd8-5568-9e5c-f9ef03f5eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1931" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}tan⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}tan⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (tan⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(tan⁡x)+({e}^{x})({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee64135e-9b9f-5429-a4df-efa522042b83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Product  at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122dcace-6bca-59bb-b96f-a96026e9a833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327088} {:answer/id #uuid "29771cef-6628-575d-b6d2-039fa89b2a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327286} {:answer/id #uuid "3101f4e9-df22-5461-be7e-f6674a765dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327368} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e4fd4c-0122-574c-8317-faf21984d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328648} {:answer/id #uuid "e154d586-179b-57cc-acf3-bc95bc04c67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3e4fd4c-0122-574c-8317-faf21984d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328648} :answer-field/id #uuid "745d0171-7216-5576-96bb-4a33b2c2f9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1066779d-ebe1-53a9-ad1f-5e9c5ee1f7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48517" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=({x}^{3}-1){e}^{x},$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{3}-1$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-1)\\cdot {e}^{x}+{e}^{x}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=2$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={{e}^{x}({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-1)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}({2}^{3}+3(2)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =19{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $19{e}^{2}.$"}]}
